-- title:
--   Splitting a distinguished monic polynomial over a complete local domain
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, Noetherian, local with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_S$, and complete with respect to the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic topology (`IsAdicComplete`), and let $P \in S[X]$ be monic with $N := \deg P > 0$ and with every coefficient $P_i$, $i < N$, lying in $\mathfrak m_S$, i.e. $P \equiv X^N$ modulo $\mathfrak m_S$. The assertion is the existence of a type $V$ carrying a commutative ring structure which is a domain, is local, is an $S$-algebra, is finite as an $S$-module and is complete for the $\mathfrak m_V$-adic topology, such that: the structure map $S \to V$ is injective; the ideal of $V$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_S$ is contained in $\mathfrak m_V$; and there is a family $r : \{0,\dots,N-1\} \to V$ with every $r_i \in \mathfrak m_V$ and $$P^{V} = \prod_{i} (X - r_i)$$ in $V[X]$, where $P^V$ denotes the image of $P$ under the coefficientwise map $S[X] \to V[X]$. The roots are indexed with multiplicity, and no claim of distinctness or of minimality of $V$ is made.
--
--   This is the splitting-ring construction for a distinguished (Weierstrass) monic polynomial over a complete Noetherian local domain: the roots of such a polynomial, which are topologically nilpotent, can be adjoined without leaving the category of module-finite complete local domains. It is used in the construction of Drinfeld bases for formal groups, being cited by [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.exists_isDomain_injective_isDrinfeldBasisAdic`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.exists_isDomain_injective_isDrinfeldBasisAdic).
